       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose, the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses of this size have also caused prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that limit.\n\nCould you confirm which of these you meant?\n\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the standard maximum.\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose. 2.5 mg is also used for frail patients or those on other antihypertensives.\n- **50 mg is intended.** If so, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Your institution's high-alert or dose-limit override process may also apply.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
